============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-space along which Pi is preserved.
  Physically: simultaneous rescaling of variables that keeps the
  normalised enthalpy Pi (and therefore the pore fraction) invariant.

  Generator 1:
    P x exp(-0.052*eps), A x exp(+0.997*eps)
    Meaning: increase A while decrease P
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 2:
    V x exp(+0.139*eps), rho x exp(+0.988*eps), gamma x exp(-0.054*eps)
    Meaning: increase rho while increase V, decrease gamma
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 3:
    P x exp(+0.167*eps), V x exp(-0.167*eps), k x exp(+0.965*eps), gamma x exp(+0.111*eps)
    Meaning: increase k while increase P, decrease V, increase gamma
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 4:
    Lv x exp(+1.000*eps)

  Generator 5:
    P x exp(+0.388*eps), k x exp(-0.064*eps), dT x exp(+0.905*eps), gamma x exp(+0.111*eps), Tb x exp(+0.107*eps)
    Meaning: increase dT while increase P, decrease k, increase gamma, increase Tb
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 6:
    P x exp(-0.121*eps), V x exp(+0.650*eps), rho x exp(-0.056*eps), dT x exp(-0.073*eps), gamma x exp(+0.740*eps), Tb x exp(+0.060*eps)
    Meaning: increase gamma while decrease P, increase V, decrease rho, decrease dT, increase Tb
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 7:
    P x exp(-0.415*eps), k x exp(+0.070*eps), dT x exp(+0.095*eps), gamma x exp(-0.133*eps), Tb x exp(+0.892*eps)
    Meaning: increase Tb while decrease P, increase k, increase dT, decrease gamma
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged


